<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmose I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1550–1525 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmose I was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a> around 1550 BCE. He completed the expulsion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> from northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and reunited the country. His reign marks the beginning of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the period of the Egyptian Empire's greatest expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ahmose-i.jpg" alt="Ahmose I" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Head_of_Ahmose_I_MET_DP140854.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Ahmose I</b>, founding pharaoh of the Eighteenth Dynasty, completed this expulsion around 1550 BCE, reunited the country, reconquered Nubian territories lost during the preceding fragmentation, and began rebuilding the administrative and military institutions that would sustain the empire for nearly five centuries.</blockquote><a href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ahmose I</b>, who came to the throne around 1550 BCE, captured Avaris some years later and then besieged Sharuhen in southern Canaan, driving out the Hyksos and founding the Egyptian Empire New Kingdom.</blockquote><a href="/state/fifteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Fifteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ahmose I</b>, probably Kamose's younger brother, came to the throne around 1550 BCE and completed the war, later taking Avaris and reuniting Egypt.</blockquote><a href="/state/seventeenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Seventeenth Dynasty of Egypt</a></li></ul></section>
